I already have the following database structure:

Article Type
    └── Article

I want to redesign it into a scalable Help Center (similar to Loyverse Help Center).

Target hierarchy:

Article Type
    └── Category (Topic)
            ├── Getting Started
            ├── Sales
            ├── Items
            ├── Inventory
            ├── Employees
            ├── Customers
            ├── Settings
            ├── Hardware
            └── Payments
                    └── Article
                            └── Sub Article
                                    └── Details

Requirements:

1. Keep the existing Article Type and Article tables.
2. Add only the necessary new tables.
3. Categories should support unlimited nesting using parent_id.
4. Articles should support unlimited sub-articles using parent_article_id.
5. One article can belong to multiple categories (many-to-many).
6. Support display_order, slug, status, icon, and description for categories.
7. Support SEO fields, summary, content, published_at, and status for articles.
8. Provide:
   - ER Diagram
   - Database schema
   - PostgreSQL DDL
   - Relationships
   - Sample data based on the Loyverse Help Center
   - Recommended indexes
9. Follow database normalization (3NF) and enterprise best practices.
10. Preserve backward compatibility with the existing Article Type → Article design as much as possible.